v3.2.3
Radon Player 3.2.3: Make it yours
## 3.2.3: Make it yours (Windows and Android)
- **Artist pictures in Search:** artists found in Search show the same picture as on the Artists tab (the one you picked, or the one looked up), and the ones not looked up yet are looked up there.
- **Lyrics card styles:** the Lyrics card box has a Style menu (by Save and the share buttons): Your look (as before), Now playing (the card as the Now playing screen looks with the Now playing look, in the cover's colours, whatever look is in use), 30 ready-made styles (Synthwave, Aurora night, Golden hour, Cherry blossom, Ocean deep, Old TV, Code rain, Galaxy, Comic book, Hyperspace and more), each with its own colours and effects, and the ones you make. Hold one or tap its ⋯ (right-click on the PC) to favourite it; yours can be edited or deleted there too. The one you pick stays for the next card.
- **Make your own lyrics card:** Settings › Personalization › Make your own › New lyrics card: every colour (the background's top and bottom, the card behind the words, the words, the song name, the soft text, the Radon Player mark), how see-through the card is and its corners, bold or regular words and their size, a round cover, stars and any effects each in its own colour. Start from any ready-made style, Copy my look, Randomize, Randomize colours and Saved colours work there too, and the card shows as you go. Yours go to your other device at each Sync and into backups.
- **Lyrics card with the Now playing look:** the card now looks like the Lyrics screen does with the Now playing look: black, the words in the cover's colour, with the stars and effects (they were left off).
- **Dual volume:** a switch under the Equalizer's Boost (the same screen from Now playing). On (as before): a song with its own volume (Volume… in its menu) gets the Boost on top too. Off: a song with its own volume plays at just that volume, without the Boost; every other song keeps the Boost.
- **Personalization presets:** Settings › Personalization has a Personalization presets menu and a Save as a preset button: it saves everything picked on the tab (look, theme, layout, the looks' own effects or the effects you picked and their colours, Now playing's visualizer) under a name, and picking a preset puts all of it back at once. Hold one or tap its ⋯ (right-click on the PC) to favourite, edit or delete it; Edit puts it on so you can change anything, then Save changes (or Save as new). Presets go to your other device at each Sync and into backups.
- **Mood scans only when you tap them:** Scan moods no longer starts by itself after your music is scanned (or after a sync); Scan moods, Full scan and Read moods from lyrics each run only when you tap them. Moods already in your files are still noticed straight away.
- **Remove all moods takes every one out:** each file is read again after its mood is taken off, and any mood still there (an MP3 tag with an extended header, an M4A's mood saved under another app's name, a FLAC with an ID3 tag in front, a file the usual writer couldn't replace) is blanked where it is, every other tag and the sound kept byte for byte. Files that still keep one are named in Settings › Problems, and moods from your other device wait until a Full scan has heard the songs here again, so a sync can't put the old ones back.
- **Your own Wrapped:** Make your own › New Wrapped: pick its background, text, soft text and accent colours and a colour for each slide, the glow (and how strong), neon text, bold or light type, text size, spacing, corners, round covers and their size, bar thickness, tiles, and stars and effects behind every slide (each effect in its own colour). Randomize, Randomize colours and Saved colours work there too, and a slide in it shows as you go.
- **Wrapped in your look:** Wrapped's Style menu has Your look: the slides take the app's look in use, its stars and effects too.
- **Favourites in Wrapped's Style menu:** hold down a style (or its ⋯, or right-click) to favourite it; the ones you made can be edited or deleted there.
- **30 more visualizers:** 15 along the bottom (City lights, Capsules, Hills, Steps, Needles, Ribbon, Dot bars, Flames, Tides, 8-bit, Bouncing balls, Meadow, Outlines, Curtain, Echoes) and 15 around the middle that come out of the cover's centre on Now playing, Full screen too (Orbits, Spiral, Polygons, Radar, Light rays, Atom, Mandala, Ripples, Supernova, Honeycomb, Heart, Sunflower, Vortex, Iris, Clockwork). They're in the Visualizer tab, Now playing's visualizer menu and Make your own visualizer.
- **Visualizers come out of the cover's middle:** a visualizer drawn around a middle (Ring, Pulse, Starfield, Dual's middle style…) now always centres on the album cover on Now playing, in every layout, with Full screen on or off.
- **Your own visualizers centre too:** one you made with Full screen on, from a style around a middle, now comes out of the cover's exact centre like the built-in ones (it's drawn from the cover itself), and the visualizer menu's previews put the cover in their middle.
- **Starfield fills the screen:** with Full screen on, its stars fly from the cover's middle out to every edge of the screen, past the song's name and the buttons, Full screen on or not (yours made from Starfield too, Dual's middle as well).
- **Dual, each its own way:** a Dual visualizer's bottom style has its own Shape it (mirror, upside down, reflection, glow, spin, strength) and its own colour, apart from the middle one's.
- **Delete stays in the menu:** deleting one of yours in a menu asks right there (Yes, delete / Cancel) and the menu stays open.
- **Everything you made is in its menu:** the list under Make your own is gone; your looks, layouts, visualizers, colour blends and Wrapped styles are in their own menus (hold or ⋯ to edit, favourite or delete; colour blends too now). Two with the same name get a number.
- **Nothing under the phone's buttons:** the bottom of every menu and full-screen page stays above the phone's Back and Home buttons, so the last ones can be tapped.
- **Your Wrapped's effects in its colours:** the effects on a Wrapped style you made (and its picture in Make your own Wrapped) are drawn in that style's own colours, not the app look's, so what you pick is what you see.
- **Make your own Wrapped shows your changes:** its pictures now change the moment you change a colour, effect, type or anything else (they stayed on the first look before).
- **The visualizer's Look's colour is your look's:** Look's colour on Now playing is your look's own colour now (it used to be turned round to a different colour); with the Now playing look it's still the cover's.
- **The PC's mini player is Now playing made small:** your look's background, stars and effects (or the cover's colours with the Now playing look), Now playing's visualizer, the cover in your layout's shape and the song, with the seek bar and buttons under it in the look's colour.
- **Rain that rains:** Rain and Code rain (and yours made from them, a Dual's bottom one too) fall down the whole of Now playing, not only the bottom.
- **Effects: look first:** on the phone the first tap on an effect shows its picture; tap it again to put it on or off.
- **Apple Music history imports a big download:** Apple's Play Activity file (hundreds of megabytes) is read a row at a time, straight from the zip, instead of all at once, which ran the phone out of memory ("Failed to allocate…"); and a stray quote mark inside a field (a 12" mix) no longer swallows the rest of the file.
- **Copy my look in Make your own Wrapped:** one tap takes your look's colours (background, text, accent, the slides in shades of it), its neon glow, stars and effects, to add your own effects and changes on top.
- **Name your saved colours:** Save these colours asks for a name straight away; hold one of yours in Saved colours (or tap its ✎) to rename it. On the phone the list ends above the phone's buttons.
- **Reset mood and lyrics scans (Settings):** Reset moods works every song's moods out again from what the scans already heard and read, dropping the moods a sync, a backup or the files brought, and rewrites them into your files, with no scanning. Reset sound scan has every song heard again (the lyrics readings kept). Clear my moods forgets the moods you picked yourself. Remove all moods takes every mood (and words' reading) out of every file and forgets everything, for a completely fresh Full scan. Only the MOOD tags ever change, nothing else in the files. The Moods tab's "heard whole" now counts only songs Full scan really heard, not ones that just have a mood in their file. Each asks if you're sure first. Moods you picked yourself stay.
- **More moods per song:** a song that's been heard is now also in the other moods that fit it fairly well, not only its main one (never its opposite, like Happy and Sad, unless that's plain).
- **30 more effects:** falling petals, autumn leaves, embers, lightning, comets, a meteor shower, a moon, a ringed planet, clouds, fog, a night sea, desert dunes, a pine forest, graph paper, polka dots, a checkerboard, plaid, a circuit board, contour lines, a starburst, a prism, sparkles, floating hearts, music notes, glowing orbs, a spiral galaxy, an old TV, glitch, warp speed and sunbeams. 61 in all, each in any colour.
- **Use the scans' moods:** songs held to the one mood already in their file (another app's, your other device's or an older version's) now show a Moods tab button to use what the scans found for them instead, with nothing heard again that was heard; the files then get all their moods. Full scan now also hears songs whose mood the app wrote itself. A song not heard on this device uses the moods your other device found (from a sync) over the single one in its file.
- **Dual's bottom style on the bottom edge:** with Full screen on, a Dual visualizer's bottom style stands right on the bottom of the screen, as a bottom style always does, not raised above it.
- **The PC's mini player has Now playing's buttons:** the song with ☆ and ⋯, the seek bar, Shuffle · previous · play · next · Repeat, the volume, and the pill with the lyrics, the output and EQ and the queue (shown in the cover's place). Only Personalization isn't there; ↑ goes back to the big window.
- **Every slide while you make your Wrapped:** Make your own Wrapped shows all your Wrapped's slides in the style you're making; swipe left and right (or ‹ ›) through them.
- **Clear of the phone's buttons:** on the phone the menus open in a box that always ends above Back and Home (it scrolls inside), and Wrapped's slides (Share… too) stay above them.

### Good to know
- **Android:** install RadonPlayer.apk over 3.2.2 (same signature, your library and settings stay), or tap Update in Settings.
- **Windows:** Radon-Player-3.2.3.msi installs over 3.2.2, or use Update in Settings.
- **Features:** the Features page (☰ menu) has everything new.
